# Retired zeta/metriplectic compatibility surface

The former contents defined a finite matrix toy in which a user-supplied zero
of an arbitrary dissipative map was renamed a "zeta zero-mode".  Its critical
line conclusion was only the scalar identity `gamma = 0`; it did not connect a
noncommutative modular flow, a zeta zero, or an entropy-production theorem.

No maintained owner depended on those definitions.  The actual operatorial
metriplectic and modular lanes are owned by:

* `InfoGeometry.Canonical.MetriplecticCore`;
* `InfoGeometry.Canonical.SouriauMetriplecticOptimalTransport`;
* the Connes/Tomita owners under `InfoGeometry.OperatorAlgebra` and
  `InfoGeometry.Canonical`.

This file remains as a docs-only import path so the obsolete scalar namespace
cannot be mistaken for a proof of a zeta resonance theorem.
-/
